%I A398550 #6 Aug 06 2026 23:23:21
%S A398550 1,2,6,60,26220,30667985460,619195022575757229178512
%N A398550 Largest value occurring in any n-tuple (x_1, ..., x_n) of distinct positive integers with 1/x_1 + 2/x_2 + ... + n/x_n = n.
%C A398550 a(n) is the point where column n of the triangle A378322 stabilizes: A378322(m,n) = A398549(n) for all m >= a(n).
%C A398550 a(n) >= 2*(n+1)^(2^(n-3)) for n >= 4 (proved). Proof sketch: assign (n-1)/1 and n/(n+1), leaving remainder 1/(n+1); then greedily assign w/x with the least admissible x for w = n-2, n-3, ..., 3, 1. A remainder 1/q always becomes 1/(q*(w*q+1)), so the denominator more than squares at each of the n-3 steps, and the final term 2/(2q) closes the sum exactly.
%C A398550 Conjecture: a(n) equals the maximum of this greedy solution for all n >= 4; verified by exhaustive enumeration for n = 4, 5, 6, 7. Under the conjecture, a(8) = 23461703336496719140483553681190653775644680508729640, and a(9) has 112 decimal digits.
%F A398550 a(n) >= 2*(n+1)^(2^(n-3)) for n >= 4.
%e A398550 a(5) = 26220, attained by the solution 4/1 + 5/6 + 3/19 + 1/115 + 2/26220 = 5.
%Y A398550 Cf. A378322, A398549.
%K A398550 nonn,hard,more
%O A398550 1,2
